{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/pulls/2","id":4083878254,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTZUlPc7zawlu","html_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback/seer/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback/seer/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback/seer/pull/2.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/issues/2","number":2,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Multi-user support: workspaces, invites, and self-serve API keys","user":{"login":"kristofferremback","id":9280031,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODAwMzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9280031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback","html_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Seer grows from one person's tool into a small shared one. Bundles now live inside a **workspace**; people are members of workspaces; every member mints, rolls, and revokes their own API keys without asking anyone.\n\n## What's in here\n\n- **Workspaces** own bundles. All members are equal — anyone can invite, anyone can change settings. Visibility is `public` (today's behavior: anyone with a link can view) or `private` (members only).\n- **API keys** are `seer_sk_` + 192 random bits, shown exactly once at mint; only the SHA-256 lives in the database. A key belongs to one (user, workspace) pair and resolves the workspace on upload — the agent-facing `PUT /api/bundles/:slug` path is unchanged, so no skills or agent configs need touching.\n- **Invites** are single-use `inv_` links with a 7-day expiry. A new user's account is created on acceptance via Google sign-in; an existing user joins the additional workspace.\n- **Serving** moves to `/<ws_id>/b/<slug>/[v/N/]`. Legacy `/b/<slug>/` links 301 into the migrated workspace, preserving version, path, and query — nothing ever shared breaks.\n- **Soft-404**: for private workspaces, forbidden and missing are byte-identical per viewer (\"Nothing here for you to see. Try signing in — there might be, who knows?\"), with the sign-in affordance only for anonymous visitors. Private bundles unfurl as a generic Seer card; titles never leak. The live-reload socket enforces the same gate.\n- **First-boot migration** (`PRAGMA user_version` 0→1, idempotent): creates the root user from `ALLOWED_EMAILS`, adopts all existing bundles and zip files into a public root workspace, and imports the env `API_KEY` as a hashed legacy key — existing agents keep working, and the imported key can be rolled from the UI without resurrecting from env.\n- **UI**: workspace-grouped ledger, settings (rename, visibility, members, invites, keys with one-time reveals), invite acceptance — all server-rendered in the existing design language, mobile-friendly at 360–390px.\n- `ALLOWED_EMAILS` retires as a login gate; the users table is the allowlist. Sessions carry the `usr_` id (everyone re-logs in once).\n\n## Testing\n\n96 tests / 491 assertions: migration (v0-with-data, fresh, no-email-fails-loudly, idempotency), key auth matrix, the public/private × anon/member/non-member visibility matrix over HTTP, legacy-redirect preservation, invite lifecycle (mint / accept-new / accept-existing / expired / reused), key lifecycle (mint / roll / revoke), upload scoping across workspaces, and page-render markers. Also verified by hand: headless screenshots of every page at 1280px and 390px against the approved design mock, with a horizontal-overflow probe.\n\nBuilt via a staged workflow (Opus builds, Opus x-high adversarially verifies each step), then a 3-perspective pre-PR review (spec compliance, correctness+security, design) — all clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-07-18T22:07:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T06:27:55Z","closed_at":"2026-07-19T06:27:51Z","merged_at":"2026-07-19T06:27:51Z","merge_commit_sha":"a5db12f5520902e442ac762a8966292b5d933904","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/pulls/2/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/pulls/2/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/issues/2/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/statuses/c1ac138dfe0268e95f006c7150833650957348c5","head":{"label":"kristofferremback:feat/support-multiple-users","ref":"feat/support-multiple-users","sha":"c1ac138dfe0268e95f006c7150833650957348c5","user":{"login":"kristofferremback","id":9280031,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODAwMzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9280031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback","html_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github